// Mutation testing of the specification algebra (forward 037, D8 item 4; docs/contratos/RELEASING.md).
// Scope: src/Specifications/ plus src/AbstractSpecification.php and src/AbstractCompositeSpecification.php;
// since 2.4.0 (forward 041) also src/Serialization/ (the specification codec); since 2.5.0 (forward 048, RN-04)
// the new and changed files of the rule engine (RuleSpecificationRegistry, DynamicSpecificationEngine,
// RulePrecedence and the two catalogs), of the TCriteria bridge (the visitor, the builder and the three new
// TFilters) and of the asynchronous data sources; since 2.6.0 (forward 045) the stage runner of the resolution
// (ResolvedData, with the deferred group of the stage transports) and DataFetchException; since 2.7.0 the new files of
// the state machine for a real consumer (MachineDefinitionDiff, the drafts and PdoMachineDefinitionRepository, the
// tenant and lister ports, the ready-made migrations and their report, DefinitionDraftConflictException) and the
// calendars of the deadlines in business time; since 2.8.0 the write-behind hybrid repository (InMemoryAndFileRepository,
// RepositoryPersistenceMetaData, IWriteBehindBackend) and the caching decorators over PSR-16 (every file of src/Cache/:
// the cached catalog, flag store and partition index, the keys, the guarded cache and the catalog version); since 2.9.0 the factory of the
// int-typed leaves (Factory/IntegerSpecificationFactory; the leaves themselves are in Specifications/); every other file of src/
// is excluded by the negative look-ahead below (a new top-level folder of src/ stays out of scope until it is
// named here). The Criteria/ classes extend Adianti's TFilter, so Infection loads tests/bootstrap.php (the stubs of the suite) itself.
// Runs in the scheduled workflow (.github/workflows/quality.yml)
// with a coverage driver (pcov); locally:
//
//   XDEBUG_MODE=off vendor/bin/infection --threads=max --only-covering-test-cases \
//       --initial-tests-php-options="-d pcov.enabled=1 -d pcov.directory=$PWD/src"
//
// minMsi / minCoveredMsi: the floor registered in RELEASING.md (measured 90.54 / 90.54 on 2026-10-19, 2.5.0, Quality workflow run 39263499101;
// Infection 0.35.8, PHP 8.4 with intl and pcov, the scope above: 4481 mutants, 4024 killed, 30 errors, 3 time-outs, 424
// escaped), a little below the measured score; a drop below it fails the run. Raise it when the score goes
// up, never lower it to make a run pass.
// 2.6.0 (forward 045): the 2.5.x scores were inflated. In a mutant process Infection replaces the file:// wrapper,
// proc_open() of Module 21's local server failed ("posix_spawn() failed: Bad file descriptor"), and every mutant
// covered by Module 21 counted as killed whatever the mutation. tests/Support/LocalHttpServer.php now redirects the
// streams in /bin/sh; measured locally (Infection 0.35.6, container, PHP 8.4 with pcov, memory_limit=2G): 4683 mutants,
// 4184 killed, 30 errors, 4 time-outs, 465 escaped, MSI 90.07 (ResolvedData 96.3, DataFetchException 100). The floor
// stays 89; the CI measurement of 2.6.0 goes to RELEASING.md on the release day.
// 2.7.0: the deadline calendars (src/StateMachine/Calendar/, every file, and UnknownDeadlineCalendarException) enter
// the scope as they are born; the changed deadline code of the core (DeadlineDefinition, StateMachine, the validator)
// is measured apart with --filter, the rest of src/StateMachine/ staying out of scope until it is named here.
// 2.10.0: the new files of the adoption of the state machine (CandidateReason, EventSnapshot, IBatchIdempotencyStore,
// BatchEvent, BatchEventOutcome, EffectContext) enter the scope as they are born; the changed lines of the core, the
// runner and the stores (StateMachine, TransitionResult, GuardRegistry, MachineRunner, the effect registry and dispatcher,
// OutboxEntry, the PDO outbox, schema and idempotency store, the in-memory idempotency store) are measured apart with
// --filter over a copy of this file without the look-ahead, as in 2.7.0.
// 2.12.0 (forward 059): the reader of Retry-After and the classification of a failed HTTP call (RetryAfter,
// HttpErrorClassification) enter the scope as they are born (DataFetchException is in it since 2.6.0); the changed
// lines of HttpDataSource (the error classifier) are measured apart with --filter, as in 2.10.0.
// 2.13.0 (forward 060): the new files of the audited writes to the rule catalog (RuleCatalogEditor, the two stores,
// RuleSnapshot, RuleRevision, RuleChangeCandidate, RuleDrift and the two enums, the seven exceptions and the two new
// contracts) enter the scope as they are born; PdoRuleCatalog, DynamicSpecificationEngine and src/Cache/ were already in
// it; the changed lines of RuleDefinition and RuleBoundSpecification are measured apart with --filter, as in 2.10.0.
// 2.14.0 (forward 063): the whole new folder src/Messaging/ (the broker-agnostic messaging hook: Message, the outbox and the
// inbox in memory and over PDO, the relay, the consumer, the in-memory transport and source, the bridges, the reports and the
// exceptions) enters the scope as it is born; nothing outside it changed.
// Measured locally (Infection 0.35.x, PHP 8.4.27 with pcov, --filter=src/Messaging, Module 48 through its bridge):
// 1011 mutants, 991 killed, 1 time-out, 19 escaped, MSI 98.12 %. The 19 are equivalent: four `= true` -> `= false` on
// arrays read with isset() only (InMemoryMessageSource 80 and 101, MessageConsumer 221 and 242, OutboxRelay 122: isset()
// of false is true); four array_values() on arrays that are already lists or are re-indexed next (InMemoryMessageTransport
// 65, MessagePublisher 81, InMemoryMessageOutbox 135, OutboxRelay 99); `< $max` -> `<= $max` in InMemoryMessageSource 71
// (array_slice() of length 0 is empty); the (string) of a reason that is never null (MessageConsumer 159) and of a VARCHAR
// read back as text by every driver (PdoMessageOutbox 240); the return of reportHandlerError() without a callback
// (MessageConsumer 291: calling null throws, and the throw is swallowed there); `':' .` of a placeholder name, which
// PDO adds itself (PdoMessageOutbox 220); the `!` of a format that sets every field (MessagingSupport 77); strlen()/`>=`
// in truncate(), where mb_substr() caps the length anyway (MessagingSupport 94, two); the PARAM_NULL and PARAM_INT arms
// (PdoMessagingTable 188: a null bound as text is NULL, an integer bound as text compares as a number in the four databases).
// 2.15.0 (forward 064): src/Messaging/Testing/ is born inside the scope of src/Messaging/, but the contract battery itself
// (MessagingContractTestCase, an abstract PHPUnit TestCase) is excluded by the second entry below, and the reason is
// recorded here: it is a test, not logic of the library. A mutant of the battery (an assertion removed, a failure message
// cut, a step of the property generator moved) is a defect of the detector, not of the hook; most of them change only what
// a failure prints, or how the random sequence is tuned, and no suite of the library can see them (measured apart, below).
// The battery is tested by the mutation of its subject instead: Module 49 runs it over the in-memory reference with 14
// planted faults, one per item of the contract, and requires the scenario of each item to fail on an assertion.
// IMessagingBench (an interface) and InMemoryMessagingBench (logic of the core, the bench over the reference) stay in scope.
// Measured apart (Infection 0.35.12, PHP 8.4.27 with pcov, --filter=src/Messaging/Testing, this file without the second
// exclude): the battery 1 139 mutants, 637 killed, 13 errors, 489
// escaped, MSI 57.07 % (the escaped ones: 252 IncrementInteger/DecrementInteger, mostly the ranges and odds of the random
// generator and the slicing of the derived ids; 106 MethodCallRemoval of assertions another one already implies; the rest
// in failure messages); counted in the scope it would take the MSI of the release below the floor of 89 with no defect of
// the library behind it. InMemoryMessagingBench, in scope: 11 mutants, 10 killed, 1 error, MSI 100 %.
// 2.16.0 (forward 065): the new files of the dispatchers in production enter the scope as they are born: the generic lease
// lock (src/Persistence/ILeaseLock, InMemoryLeaseLock, PdoLeaseLock, LeaseLockException, LeaseLockSupport) and the three
// retention interfaces (Messaging/Outbox/IMessageOutboxRetention is inside Messaging/ already;
// DomainEvents/Outbox/IDomainEventOutboxRetention and StateMachine/Persistence/IEffectOutboxRetention are named below);
// the changed lines of the domain event and effect dispatchers, their reports and their four outboxes (DomainEvents/,
// StateMachine/) are measured apart with --filter over a copy of this file without the look-ahead, as in 2.10.0.
// Measured apart (2.16.0, Infection 0.35.12, PHP 8.4.27 with pcov, --filter over the 16 files born or changed, whole files):
// 1 072 mutants, 938 killed, 1 error, 9 timeouts, 124 escaped, MSI 88.43 % (58 of the escaped on lines older than 2.16.0).
{
    "$schema": "vendor/infection/infection/resources/schema.json",
    "source": {
        "directories": ["src"],
        "excludes": [
            "~^(?!Specifications/|Serialization/|AbstractSpecification\\.php$|AbstractCompositeSpecification\\.php$|Engine/(?:RuleSpecificationRegistry|DynamicSpecificationEngine|RulePrecedence|InMemoryRuleCatalog|PdoRuleCatalog)\\.php$|Criteria/(?:TAccentInsensitiveFilter|TSubqueryFilter|TConstantFilter|TCriteriaBuilder|CriteriaSpecificationVisitor)\\.php$|Resolution/(?:AsyncDataSource|AsyncPoll|AsyncTicket|CallableAsyncTicketStore|InMemoryAsyncTicketStore|IAsyncTicketStore)\\.php$|Resolution/ResolvedData\\.php$|Resolution/(?:RetryAfter|HttpErrorClassification)\\.php$|Resolution/Exceptions/(?:DataPendingException|DataFetchException)\\.php$|StateMachine/MachineDefinitionDiff\\.php$|StateMachine/Persistence/(?:DefinitionDraftSupport|DraftInfo|MachineDefinitionDraft|PublishedMachineDefinition|IMachineDefinitionDrafts|ITenantScopedInstanceStore|IMachineInstanceLister)\\.php$|StateMachine/Persistence/Pdo/PdoMachineDefinitionRepository\\.php$|StateMachine/Runner/(?:ByStateNameMigration|MachineMigrations|InstanceMigration|IDefinitionAwareMachineMigration)\\.php$|StateMachine/Exceptions/DefinitionDraftConflictException\\.php$|StateMachine/Calendar/|StateMachine/Exceptions/UnknownDeadlineCalendarException\\.php$|Cache/|Repositories/RepositoryPersistenceMetaData\\.php$|Repositories/File/InMemoryAndFileRepository\\.php$|Contracts/Repositories/IWriteBehindBackend\\.php$|Factory/IntegerSpecificationFactory\\.php$|StateMachine/CandidateReason\\.php$|StateMachine/Persistence/(?:EventSnapshot|IBatchIdempotencyStore)\\.php$|StateMachine/Runner/(?:BatchEvent|BatchEventOutcome|EffectContext)\\.php$|Engine/(?:RuleCatalogEditor|RuleRevision|RuleChangeKind|RuleChangeCandidate|RuleDrift|RuleDriftKind|RuleSnapshot|PdoRuleCatalogStore|InMemoryRuleCatalogStore)\\.php$|Engine/Exceptions/(?:RuleCatalogEditorException|StaleRuleChangeException|RuleChangeRefusedException|RuleCatalogStoreException|RuleNotFoundException|RuleCatalogDriftException|InvalidRuleChangeReasonException)\\.php$|Contracts/Engine/(?:IVersionedRuleDefinition|IRuleCatalogStore)\\.php$|Messaging/|Persistence/(?:ILeaseLock|InMemoryLeaseLock|PdoLeaseLock|LeaseLockException|LeaseLockSupport)\\.php$|DomainEvents/Outbox/IDomainEventOutboxRetention\\.php$|StateMachine/Persistence/IEffectOutboxRetention\\.php$)~",
            "~^Messaging/Testing/MessagingContractTestCase\\.php$~"
        ]
    },
    "bootstrap": "tests/bootstrap.php",
    "timeout": 120,
    "logs": {
        "text": "coverage/infection/infection.log",
        "summary": "coverage/infection/summary.log",
        "json": "coverage/infection/infection.json",
        "perMutator": "coverage/infection/per-mutator.md"
    },
    "tmpDir": "coverage/infection/tmp",
    "phpUnit": {
        "configDir": "."
    },
    "mutators": {
        "@default": true
    },
    "minMsi": 89,
    "minCoveredMsi": 89
}
